  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0209 database is designed to manage information about students, courses, classes, teachers, and departments within an educational institution. The students table stores details about each student, including their ID, first name, middle name, last name, date of birth, email, phone number, address, and a description of the student. The courses table contains information about each course, such as its ID, name, code, creation date, credit hours, and a description. The enrollments table links students to courses they are enrolled in, with each enrollment having a unique ID, the student's ID, the course ID, the enrollment date, and a description. The classes table stores details about each class, including its ID, course ID, name, schedule, room, and a description. The attendance table tracks student attendance in classes, with each attendance record containing a unique ID, the class ID, the student ID, the attendance date, a status, and a description. The grades table stores the marks obtained by students in each course, with each grade record having a unique ID, the enrollment ID, the marks obtained, the total marks, the grade, and a description. The teachers table stores information about each teacher, including their ID, first name, middle name, last name, email, phone number, address, and a description. The teaching assignments table links teachers to classes they teach, with each assignment having a unique ID, the teacher ID, the class ID, and a description. The departments table stores information about each department, including its ID and name, along with a description. The student department table links students to the departments they belong to, with each record containing a description, the student ID, and the department ID. The relationships between these tables are established through foreign keys, ensuring that data integrity is maintained, for example, a student can only be enrolled in a course that exists in the courses table, and a teacher can only teach a class that exists in the classes table.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nThe project is focused on developing a comprehensive database system for managing student records and associated academic activities. This database, known as `StudentManagement`, is designed to handle various aspects of student data, including courses, grades, attendance, and departmental affiliations.\n\nObjectives\n\nThe primary objective is to implement a robust database framework that facilitates efficient management of student information, course enrollments, grading systems, and attendance tracking. The system should provide functionalities for student registration, record maintenance, and academic performance evaluation.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- Students: Access their personal and academic information.\n- Teachers: Manage class schedules, assignments, and record student performance.\n- Administrators: Oversee the database, manage student enrollments, and ensure data integrity.\n- Departments: Monitor departmental data and student affiliations.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. Student Registration: \n   - Functions to add, update, and manage student personal and contact information.\n   - Linking students to their respective departments.\n\n2. Course Management:\n   - Creation and management of courses, including course schedules and room assignments.\n\n3. Enrollment Management:\n   - Enroll students in courses and maintain enrollment records.\n\n4. Grade Tracking:\n   - Record student grades and calculate their academic performance based on obtained marks.\n\n5. Attendance Tracking:\n   - Maintain attendance records for students in each class.\n\n6. Teaching Assignments:\n   - Manage teacher assignments to classes and provide relevant class information.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: Support a growing number of student records and courses without degradation in performance.\n- Data Integrity: Ensure consistency and accuracy of student and academic records.\n- Security: Protect sensitive student data from unauthorized access.\n- Availability: The system should be available for access by students, teachers, and administrators at all required times.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0209.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0209\nCREATE TABLE `students` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `middle_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `date_of_birth` date NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `courses` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `credit_hours` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `enrollments` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `enrollment_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `enrollments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`student_id`) REFERENCES `students` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `enrollments_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`course_id`) REFERENCES `courses` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `classes` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `schedule` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `room` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `classes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`course_id`) REFERENCES `courses` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `attendance` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `class_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `attendance_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `attendance_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`class_id`) REFERENCES `classes` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `attendance_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`student_id`) REFERENCES `students` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `grades` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `enrollment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `marks_obtained` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL,\n  `total_marks` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL,\n  `grade` varchar(2) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `grades_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`enrollment_id`) REFERENCES `enrollments` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `teachers` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `middle_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `teaching_assignments` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `teacher_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `class_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `teaching_assignments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`teacher_id`) REFERENCES `teachers` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `teaching_assignments_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`class_id`) REFERENCES `classes` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `departments` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `student_department` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`, `department_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `student_department_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`student_id`) REFERENCES `students` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `student_department_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `departments` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
